{# A section heading inside a page. Sized well below the page's own title so
   the two are not competing: this names a group of questions, it is not the
   thing the visitor is being asked. #}
{# `focus:outline-none` because theme/js/intake.js focuses the new page's
   first heading on every step change, to announce it ([25.14]). That focus is
   programmatic and the heading is not interactive, so the ring the browser
   draws for it points at nothing the visitor can act on -- it read as a text
   box drawn around the section title. Keyboard focus rings elsewhere are
   untouched; nothing can tab to this. #}
<h2 tabindex="-1" class="font-heading text-lg font-bold leading-tight text-heading focus:outline-none{% if field.runtime_class %} {{ field.runtime_class }}{% endif %}">{{ field.label }}</h2>
{% if field.description %}
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ field.description }}</p>
{% endif %}
